  "categories": {
    "rRNA": {
      "description": "The 29 nuclear loci GENCODE types rRNA and that no external authority contradicts: the seventeen 5S array genes RNA5S1 through RNA5S17 at 1q42.13, the three acrocentric 5.8S genes RNA5-8SN1 through RNA5-8SN3 at 21p11.2, and nine unsymbolised RFAM 5S and 5.8S loci. Every member is expected to be transcribed as ribosomal RNA. Be aware that GENCODE annotates no 18S and no 28S gene anywhere in human: RNA45SN1 and RNA18SN1 are HGNC-approved but carry no Ensembl gene id at all. Summing this category therefore yields a 5S and 5.8S fraction only, and misses the 18S and 28S species that dominate real rRNA contamination in RNA-seq.",
      "source": "GENCODE release 50 gene_type=rRNA from the registered GTF, minus every locus whose HGNC-approved symbol marks it a pseudogene. The retained symbolised genes were checked at rest.genenames.org, which gives locus_type \"RNA, ribosomal\" for RNA5S1, RNA5S17, RNA5-8SN1 and RNA5-8SN3, and against Ensembl REST, whose biotype and coordinates match the GTF row to the base. The unsymbolised 5S_rRNA and 5_8S_rRNA entries carry only an RFAM source, RF00001 and RF00002, which no other publisher disputes, so GENCODE's own call stands for those.",
