    "rRNA_pseudogene": {
      "description": "An rRNA-derived nuclear locus not expected to yield functional rRNA. It holds every locus GENCODE types rRNA_pseudogene, plus the eighteen loci GENCODE types rRNA whose HGNC-approved symbol is a 5S ribosomal pseudogene symbol and whose functional status is therefore disputed between publishers.",
      "source": "GENCODE release 50 gene_type=rRNA_pseudogene from the registered GTF, plus the eighteen gene_type=rRNA loci whose gene_name falls in the HGNC pseudogene series RNA5SP<n>. HGNC records those with locus_group \"pseudogene\" while Ensembl carries the biotype rRNA, and the conservative reading of a disputed functional status puts them here rather than in rRNA; HGNC was checked at rest.genenames.org for RNA5SP150, RNA5SP343, RNA5SP524 and RNA5SP536. Read verbatim, this GTF's gene_type attribute gives 47 rRNA and 497 rRNA_pseudogene, the counts recorded in issue #111. The 29 and 515 shipped here differ from those by exactly that HGNC-symbol correction and by nothing else.",
